From: MaSi-OS <masies@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mhi: drain event rings and start AMSS from SBL poll

KERNEL #4 reached "Polled EE SBL, queueing AMSS download" then never
logged BHIe or wlan. BHIe completion is MMIO, but WCN7850 on 7.2.8 also
needs the host to process event rings (MSI still dead) and the SBL
worker skipped AMSS when ee was already SBL.

Poll-drain event rings during BHI/BHIe waits, run AMSS/BHIe inline when
SBL is observed, then keep polling for Mission mode.

Applied in-tree by scripts/apply-masi-72-overlays.py (linux-7.2.x). GNU
patch cannot carry this: the original commit message had no diff, and
the SBL worker must still run AMSS download (do not skip when EE is
already SBL). Content-present skip in lib/kbuild/patches.sh:
mhi_drain_events + "Mission mode M0, creating devices".

Signed-off-by: MaSi-OS <masies@local>
